title: Role::JSON's engine encoder has no convert_blessed, while five value objects'
  POD calls it 'the house default'
updated: 2026-09-01T19:19:20Z
---

Found while making Langertha::Response.created a Langertha::Moment (karr #117 / GH #3).

Langertha::Usage, Langertha::Cost, Langertha::ToolChoice, Langertha::Tool, Langertha::ToolCall
and Langertha::UsageRecord each carry the same POD comment above their TO_JSON:

    # convert_blessed => 1 (the house default, see Langertha::Plugin::Langfuse).

That is true of Langertha::Plugin::Langfuse (lib/Langertha/Plugin/Langfuse.pm:210 builds
JSON::MaybeXS->new(utf8 => 1, canonical => 1, convert_blessed => 1)) but NOT of the engine
encoder every engine actually uses:

    lib/Langertha/Role/JSON.pm:45
      sub _build__json { JSON::MaybeXS->new( utf8 => 1, canonical => 1 ) }

So $engine->json->encode dies on any blessed value ("encountered object ..., but neither
allow_blessed, convert_blessed nor allow_tags settings are enabled"). Today that is latent,
not broken: the request bodies it encodes never contain value objects, and
Role::Langfuse:480 ($self->json->encode({ batch => $batch })) is only reached with plain
strings from the internal call sites. But langfuse_update_trace / _span / _generation take
$opts{output} from the caller, and a caller passing a Langertha::Response there hits the
croak — as would any user reaching for $engine->json as a convenience encoder.

Two ways to reconcile, both cheap:
  (a) add convert_blessed => 1 to Role::JSON::_build__json, making the POD true; or
  (b) fix the six POD comments to name Plugin::Langfuse as the only encoder that enables it.

(a) is the safer default and matches what every value object in the distribution already
assumes about how it gets serialized. Deliberately NOT done as a drive-by inside the
created/Time::Moment change: it touches the encoder every engine builds every request with.

Fixed in b9ec772 via option (a): convert_blessed => 1 on Role::JSON::_build__json, making the six value objects' 'house default' POD true on the engine encoder. Request-body encoding unchanged (plain data). Gated by a round-trip test through a real engine->json.

Orchestrator review 2026-09-01: diff b9ec772 verified. convert_blessed on the engine encoder, round-trip test through a real engine->json. Request bodies unaffected. Closing.
